/*
 * manifest.def — the curriculum, in order.
 *
 * This file is an "X-macro" list. It is included more than once, each time
 * with the two macros below defined to mean something different: once to
 * declare the lesson symbols, once to build the dispatch table. One list,
 * two expansions, no possibility of the two drifting apart.
 *
 * You will write an X-macro yourself in about_preprocessor. Until then, know
 * that this is a genuine, load-bearing C idiom and not a trick.
 *
 * Order matters. Each lesson assumes everything above it.
 */

